> Take Nera's shop door to Nera's shop floor   [success, watch 1]
> Ask Nera how to prepare   [success, watch 2]
  "'Plan your way back before you go down,' says Nera. 'Maud's pallets are two coin. I sell what I have, and when it is gone it is gone. Antidote treats poison, not a crushed skull. Take a line; there are clefts in that hill that strength alone won't get you across.'"
  | Bunches of herbs hang from the beams over shelves of jars, coils of rope, stoppered antidotes and wrapped rations.
> Buy Antidote for Dori · 3 coin   [success, watch 3]
  "Nera takes the money and hands Antidote to Dori."
  ~ Dori gains 1 Antidote.
> Take Nera's shop door to Reedwake quay   [success, watch 4]
  * Wren hurries over to you. 'Are you going up to Censer Hill foundry? Have you seen Pell?'
> Take the shrine porch to the shrine   [success, watch 5]
> Ask Iven about the keepers' dead   [success, watch 6]
  "'We are the Keepers of Names,' says Iven. 'We do not command the dead or what guards them; we hold them in custody. Our register was lost in the flood, and without it the dead are only bones to anyone with a pry bar. If the register survives, bring me word of it and I will write you a custody writ. Our guardians honour the writ. Killing them also opens the way, but then there is no keeper below at all.'"
> Ask Iven about the salvage   [success, watch 7]
  "'Edda has a permit for machinery,' says Iven. 'Not for Named vault. If anything that was buried with the dead comes up for sale, I will hear of it.'"
> Take the shrine porch to Reedwake quay   [success, watch 8]
> Ask Wren what is wrong   [success, watch 9]
  "'Pell went up to Censer Hill foundry at first light and should have been back by mid-morning,' says Wren. 'Nobody has seen them since. The short way in is the drain culvert, and the rising river will close it at about watch 34; after that you go the long way round. Please. Go and look.'"
== EXPLORATION
> Take the causeway path to Willow causeway   [success, watch 15]
  | Old stones run out across the floodplain between willow poles. Waterfowl lift from the sedges. A track climbs the chalk ridge; a lower path drops into the reeds.
  | A boar has rooted up the low path and stands across it, bristling, watching you.
> Read a reedbank boar's warning posture and give it room   [success, watch 16]
> Take the low path through the reeds to Drain mouth   [success, watch 19]
> Take the drain culvert to Bell workshop   [success, watch 20]
  | A split pipe hisses over the boiler arch. Fresh scorch marks stripe the boiler arch; turning its seized valve needs a crowbar. A fire ward can blunt a scald, but the jet must still be crossed.
  | A rusted padlock holds the stores door shut.
  | Half-cast bells lean against the walls. Chalk circles mark reusable bronze; older burial marks below the stores door declare another custody. Doorways lead to the stores and the vestibule; steps go down to the casting gallery, and the culvert mouth gapes in the floor.
  | The drain culvert is still clear, but the rising river will close it at about watch 34.
