== RESCUE
> Take the hoist passage to Hoist room   [success, watch 32]
  * A voice from low down in the dark: 'Here! Over here. Mind the fallen timber rack; it's on my leg. Don't just haul on it. Something cracked when it came down.'
  | An uncovered counterweight hangs over the shaft. It releases when the cable takes weight.
  | A slack cable hangs from the hoist drum. Timber and tools lie where a rack came down. The shaft drops to the refuge.
  | Pell lies half under the fallen timber rack, one leg trapped beneath it. Their face is grey with pain and cold.
  | The fallen timber rack lies across the floor where it fell, wedged against the wall.
  | The bronze tram bearing lies here, stamped with Edda's chalk.
